<h2>Welcome to the TimeCal beta</h2>
<p>The first self-updating build. TimeCal now checks for updates daily and
installs them in place, so this is the last version you'll ever download by
hand. You can check manually any time via <b>File &gt; Check for Updates…</b></p>

<h2>What TimeCal is</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Every calendar on your Mac, on one butter-smooth timeline: pan and
        zoom from years down to minutes.</li>
    <li>Direct-manipulation editing with explicit save: drag, resize,
        duplicate, paint new events; nothing commits until you confirm.</li>
    <li>Bookmarks (including locked multi-range views), an event template
        library, calendar groups, and pinned floating event cards.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Feedback</h2>
<p>Send anything, bugs, ideas, confusion, to
<a href="mailto:evan@sandpipermediagroup.com">evan@sandpipermediagroup.com</a>.</p>

